{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-205207-r4519021","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Sweet and Sour Pork Loin","sourcePageId":205207,"sourceRevision":"4519021","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T17:20:18Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Sweet%20and%20Sour%20Pork%20Loin&oldid=4519021","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:07.130Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Asian recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using Thai chile","Category:Recipes using coconut milk","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using ketchup","Category:Recipes using light brown sugar","Category:Recipes using pork","Category:Recipes using soy sauce","Category:Recipes using vinegar","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Roasted recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"04141259c19f9443be462cbdcec6561a78145d5f582bcb4f4897be1fca090e3f","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Meat recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n== Ingredients ==\n*1 [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. (4 [[Cookbook:Pound|pounds]] / 1.8 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]]) boneless [[Cookbook:Pork#Loin|pork loin]] roast\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*¾ cup [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]]\n*2 cups [[Cookbook:Coconut Milk|coconut milk]]\n*2 cups water\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]] [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n*2 tbsp minced [[Cookbook:ginger|ginger]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Ketchup|ketchup]]\n*1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Sesame Oil|sesame oil]]\n*¼ cup rice wine [[Cookbook:Vinegar|vinegar]]\n*¼ cup light [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n*1 ½ Thai [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]], finely minced \n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine salt, honey, water, and coconut milk in a gallon-size zip-top bag. Add pork roast and toss to coat; refrigerate 2½–3 hours.\n#Drain pork and pat dry with [[Cookbook:Paper Towel|paper towels]]. Discard remaining brine.\n#Combine ketchup, vinegar, oil, and soy sauce. Toss pork roast in mixture and place on a roasting rack in a roasting pan.\n#Combine remaining ingredients and press into all sides of pork. Insert a probe [[Cookbook:Thermometer|thermometer]] into the center and bake in a 425°F (220°C) [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] until internal temperature reaches 140°F (60°C) for medium rare.\n#Move to a plate and let rest 7 minutes. Serve warm with sweet and sour sauce on the side.\n\n\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vinegar]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Roasted recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Asian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using light brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using Thai chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using soy sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ketchup]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Sweet and Sour Pork Loin","nameAr":null,"servings